1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,275
Mixing the Service.

2
00:00:02,225 --> 00:00:06,512
Follow the service flow — know what to unmute, lower, and when.

3
00:00:06,512 --> 00:00:08,337
Service Flow.

4
00:00:08,337 --> 00:00:11,225
Walk-in: Playback music on low.

5
00:00:11,225 --> 00:00:13,125
All mics muted.

6
00:00:13,125 --> 00:00:15,775
Create a welcoming atmosphere.

7
00:00:15,775 --> 00:00:20,462
Welcome / Announcements: Unmute the speaker's mic BEFORE they step up.

8
00:00:20,462 --> 00:00:22,487
Lower the music.

9
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:24,737
Keep other mics muted.

10
00:00:24,737 --> 00:00:27,775
Worship: Bring up band and vocals.

11
00:00:27,775 --> 00:00:31,312
Lead vocal should sit clearly on top of the mix.

12
00:00:31,312 --> 00:00:34,237
Prayer & Offering: Bring band down.

13
00:00:34,237 --> 00:00:36,837
Keep one mic live for the leader.

14
00:00:36,837 --> 00:00:39,362
Mute instruments that stopped.

15
00:00:39,362 --> 00:00:42,662
Sermon: Pastor mic is the PRIORITY.

16
00:00:42,662 --> 00:00:45,312
Mute everything else not in use.

17
00:00:45,312 --> 00:00:48,012
Full focus on speech clarity.

18
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:51,850
Closing: Unmute closing speakers/musicians.

19
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:55,787
Bring walk-out music back in gradually after dismissal.

20
00:00:55,787 --> 00:00:59,575
Good habit: Unmute a mic just before someone speaks.

21
00:00:59,575 --> 00:01:02,437
Make small, smooth fader moves.

22
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:05,275
Mute mics immediately when done.

23
00:01:05,275 --> 00:01:07,475
Clean in, clean out.

24
00:01:07,475 --> 00:01:09,587
When You Hear Feedback.

25
00:01:09,587 --> 00:01:14,737
Pull the ringing mic's fader down quickly: Not all the way — just enough to stop the ring.

26
00:01:14,737 --> 00:01:17,262
Find the culprit and pull it.

27
00:01:17,262 --> 00:01:18,987
Can't find it?

28
00:01:18,987 --> 00:01:23,050
Mute unused mics: Mute any mic not actively in use.

29
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:27,137
Feedback almost always comes from an open, unused mic..

30
00:01:27,137 --> 00:01:31,700
Don't touch the main LR fader: Pulling main LR kills all sound.

31
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:35,000
That's usually worse than a moment of feedback.

32
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:41,112
Tell the sound lead after service: Feedback signals a gain or EQ issue worth fixing before next Sunday.

